From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:00:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lavf/oggparsevorbis: set stream start_time before applying
 ts_offset

Commit 63b7e4cefa91 stopped setting st->start_time on the BOS page while
shifting the priming packet's timestamp by -ts_offset. Because the priming
packet produces no PCM output, actual audio begins at the unshifted
timestamp (0). Leaving start_time unset caused ogg_get_length() to subtract
the negative pts from st->duration (inflating duration by ts_offset) and
update_initial_timestamps() to set a negative start_time.

Set st->start_time to os->lastpts on the BOS page before subtracting
priv->ts_offset.

Backport of upstream 1d83e7145c258730c09ae7e7d2b0eabc5e148571. The
limited_input_seek reference differs at this base and the
ogg-vorbis-ts-seek-1.5s test does not exist here, so those reference
updates are dropped.
